      },
      "ScoreRow": {
        "description": "One row of a candidate's star-score breakdown (spec \u00a74.7).\n\nEight of these reconstruct the score arithmetically next to the chart \u2014 the\ndimension's name, its weight (2 for tightness and orderliness, 1 for the rest)\nand whether it hit. ``n/10 \u2192 stars`` is ``sum(weight where hit) \u00f7 2``.",
        "properties": {
          "dimension": {
            "title": "Dimension",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "hit": {
            "title": "Hit",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "weight": {
            "title": "Weight",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "dimension",
          "weight",
          "hit"
        ],
        "title": "ScoreRow",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "SectorDetailResponse": {
        "description": "The member list behind one sector \u2014 the drill-down (spec \u00a75.5 / \u00a74.5).\n\n``sector`` echoes the resolved label (the path segment is URL-encoded, GECS\nlabels carrying spaces such as ``Consumer Cyclical``). ``members`` is sorted\nby symbol; it is empty when no run has published (``session`` is ``None``, the\nexplicit empty state) or when a valid sector simply has no members tonight.\n``taxonomy`` is always ``\"GECS\"`` (\u00a72.6).",
        "properties": {
          "market": {
            "title": "Market",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "members": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SectorMember"
            },
            "title": "Members",
            "type": "array"
          },
          "sector": {
            "title": "Sector",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "session": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "format": "date",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Session"
          },
          "taxonomy": {
            "const": "GECS",
            "default": "GECS",
            "title": "Taxonomy",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "market",
          "session",
          "sector",
          "members"
        ],
        "title": "SectorDetailResponse",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "SectorMember": {
        "description": "One name inside a sector's drill-down (spec \u00a75.5).\n\nThe member list behind a sector row: what the Sectors screen drills into. A\nmember is a universe name carrying this sector's label that appears in the\nsession's rank table, so every field is read off that table (\u00a74.3) \u2014 nothing\nis recomputed here.\n\nPhase-1 fields, all per-lookback so the client's lookback switch re-renders\nwithout a refetch: ``returns`` (the raw per-lookback return), ``pctile_universe``\n(the percentile, **named for its population** \u2014 this repo ranks over the whole\nuniverse, applying no tradability filter, so the field must not borrow a name\nthat means ``gated`` elsewhere), and ``top_decile`` (whether the name is in\nthat lookback's top decile, ``percentile \u2265 TOP_DECILE`` \u2014 the per-name decile\nbadge, P1). A lookback the name is not ranked in (a recent listing) is simply\nabsent from all three maps.\n\nPhase-2 fields, typed nullable and always ``None`` today:\n- ``pct_of_52w_high`` \u2014 no 52-week high is computed anywhere yet (\u00a71.3).\n- ``verdict`` \u2014 the detector's grade, where **``None`` means *not evaluated***,\n  a different fact from ``extended`` (spec \u00a72.1): a pack contains names the\n  detector never ran on.",
        "properties": {
          "pct_of_52w_high": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "number"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Pct Of 52W High"
          },
          "pctile_universe": {
            "additionalProperties": {
              "type": "number"
            },
            "title": "Pctile Universe",
            "type": "object"
          },
          "returns": {
            "additionalProperties": {
              "type": "number"
            },
            "title": "Returns",
            "type": "object"
          },
          "symbol": {
            "title": "Symbol",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "top_decile": {
            "additionalProperties": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "title": "Top Decile",
            "type": "object"
          },
          "verdict": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Verdict"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "symbol",
          "returns",
          "pctile_universe",
          "top_decile",
          "pct_of_52w_high",
          "verdict"
        ],
        "title": "SectorMember",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "SectorStrength": {
        "description": "One sector's leadership and rotation numbers (spec \u00a74.4 / ticket 07 S2\u2013S8).\n\n``shares`` carries the five per-lookback strengths \u2014 the share of this\nsector's members in that lookback's top decile, ``k/n``. ``members`` is\n``n`` (the sector's universe count) and ``decile_counts`` is ``k`` per\nlookback, so the UI can render the ``k/n`` fragility badge (S4).",
        "properties": {
          "decile_counts": {
            "additionalProperties": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "title": "Decile Counts",
            "type": "object"
          },
          "delta_low_confidence": {
            "title": "Delta Low Confidence",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "members": {
            "title": "Members",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "rotation_eligible": {
            "title": "Rotation Eligible",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "sector": {
            "title": "Sector",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "shape_differential": {
            "title": "Shape Differential",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "shares": {
            "additionalProperties": {
              "type": "number"
            },
            "title": "Shares",
            "type": "object"
          },
          "temporal_delta": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "number"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Temporal Delta"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "sector",
          "members",
          "shares",
          "decile_counts",
          "shape_differential",
          "temporal_delta",
          "rotation_eligible",
          "delta_low_confidence"
        ],
        "title": "SectorStrength",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "SectorsResponse": {
        "description": "The sector board and the ranked-industry board for one market (\u00a74.4).\n\n``sectors`` is always the full 11-sector axis, default-sorted by shape\ndifferential with the rotation-ineligible sectors grouped below (S4/S8).\n``industries`` carries only the ``members \u2265 10`` rows. ``session`` is the\nas-of published session, ``None`` when no run has published.",
        "properties": {
          "industries": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/IndustryStrength"
            },
            "title": "Industries",
            "type": "array"
          },
          "market": {
            "title": "Market",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "sectors": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SectorStrength"
            },
            "title": "Sectors",
            "type": "array"
          },
          "session": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "format": "date",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Session"
          },
          "taxonomy": {
            "const": "GECS",
            "default": "GECS",
            "title": "Taxonomy",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "market",
          "session",
          "sectors",
          "industries"
        ],
        "title": "SectorsResponse",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "SetupOverlay": {
        "description": "The setup drawn on top of the candles (spec \u00a75.1 / \u00a73.5 / ticket 41) \u2014 the\nchart as *evidence for the score*, not merely a price chart.\n\n- ``base_start`` / ``cluster_start`` are the first sessions of the base and of\n  the tight trailing cluster inside it; the frontend shades each region from\n  its start to the last candle (the base always ends today, \u00a74.5).\n- ``trigger`` (cluster high) and ``stop`` (the proposed convention stop line,\n  issue #127) are the two horizontal rules \u00a77's affordability test is read off\n  geometrically.\n- ``envelope`` is the fitted upper line drawn **as a line series** so candles\n  pierce it in both directions \u2014 per \u00a73.2 that is the correct picture and must\n  not be \"fixed\" in rendering. Anchored at the cluster's max-high bar with the\n  detection's non-positive slope, so it can never exceed the trigger.\n- ``score`` (0\u20135 stars) and ``breakdown`` (the eight \u00a74.7 dimensions, each with\n  its weight and hit) reconstruct the sort key arithmetically beside the chart.\n\n``None`` for the whole overlay when the name has no detection tonight \u2014 there\nis no base to shade, no envelope to fit and no score to break down.",
        "properties": {
          "base_start": {
            "format": "date",
            "title": "Base Start",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "breakdown": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ScoreRow"
            },
            "title": "Breakdown",
            "type": "array"
          },
          "cluster_start": {
            "format": "date",
            "title": "Cluster Start",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "envelope": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MaPoint"
            },
            "title": "Envelope",
            "type": "array"
          },
          "score": {
            "title": "Score",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "stop": {
            "title": "Stop",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "trigger": {
            "title": "Trigger",
            "type": "number"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "base_start",
          "cluster_start",
          "trigger",
          "stop",
          "envelope",
          "score",
          "breakdown"
        ],
        "title": "SetupOverlay",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "ValidationError": {
        "properties": {
          "ctx": {
            "title": "Context",
            "type": "object"
          },
          "input": {
            "title": "Input"
          },
          "loc": {
            "items": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "integer"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Location",
            "type": "array"
          },
          "msg": {
            "title": "Message",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": {
            "title": "Error Type",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "loc",
          "msg",
          "type"
        ],
        "title": "ValidationError",
        "type": "object"
      }
    }
  },
  "info": {
    "title": "Qullamaggie Screening Dashboard",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/api/candidates/{market}": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "get_candidates_api_candidates__market__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "market",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Market",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CandidatesResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get Candidates"
      }
    },
    "/api/chart/{market}/{symbol}": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "get_chart_api_chart__market___symbol__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "market",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Market",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "symbol",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Symbol",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "bars",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "minimum": 1,
                  "type": "integer"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "title": "Bars"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ChartResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get Chart"
      }
    },
    "/api/leaders/{market}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "The five leaderboards for one market (spec \u00a74.4).",
        "operationId": "get_leaders_api_leaders__market__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "market",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Market",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/LeadersResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get Leaders"
      }
    },
    "/api/regime/{market}": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "get_regime_api_regime__market__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "market",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Market",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RegimeResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get Regime"
      }
    },
    "/api/runs/{market}": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "get_runs_api_runs__market__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "market",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Market",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RunsResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get Runs"
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "trigger_run_api_runs__market__post",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "market",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Market",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "description": "Operator override (issue #111): re-pull and replace a published session after an enumeration fix, instead of the ordinary run-on-open. The swap only lands if the fresh pull clears the completeness gate, so a throttled retry cannot downgrade good data.",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "recompute",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": false,
              "description": "Operator override (issue #111): re-pull and replace a published session after an enumeration fix, instead of the ordinary run-on-open. The swap only lands if the fresh pull clears the completeness gate, so a throttled retry cannot downgrade good data.",
              "title": "Recompute",
              "type": "boolean"
            }
          },
          {
            "description": "The session to recompute (default: last final). Ignored unless recompute=true.",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "session",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "format": "date",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "The session to recompute (default: last final). Ignored unless recompute=true.",
              "title": "Session"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RunTriggerResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Trigger Run"
      }
    },
    "/api/sectors/{market}": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "get_sectors_api_sectors__market__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "market",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Market",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SectorsResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get Sectors"
      }
    },
    "/api/sectors/{market}/{sector}": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "get_sector_detail_api_sectors__market___sector__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "market",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Market",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "sector",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Sector",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SectorDetailResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get Sector Detail"
      }
    }
  }
}
